# Multi-tenancy (CRITICAL)

Tenancy is ROW-LEVEL in a shared database. Never use schema-per-tenant.

- Tenant-scoped models carry `community_id` AND denormalized `city_id`.
- City-shared models (housing, community exchange/marketplace, city-wide partners)
  carry `city_id` ONLY — never `community_id`.
- Partners have `scope = community | city_wide`.
- NEVER write a tenant-scoped query without the tenant filter. Use the tenant-aware
  default manager / middleware; do not rely on remembering to filter manually.
- Before any query, decide: community-isolated or city-shared? Filter accordingly.
- Members of one community must NEVER read another community's isolated data.
- Every feature must be designed so a new community in an existing city instantly
  sees that city's shared housing/marketplace/city-wide partners.